{
  "version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "comment": "engine.freight (MOD-047, §33/§8) — the freight harbour, tonnes accounting and production-chain data contract. Every tunable figure the freight module consumes — port berths/crane-rate/hours, customs throughput, the modal per-movement bulk caps, storage-site capacities, the freight-commodity taxonomy and its market/storage mapping, and the five production-chain families' per-stage input/output rates, jobs, power/water draw and blight class — lives here, never as a Go literal in internal/engine/freight/*.go (GR#15).",
    "unitConvention": "All freight tonnage is accounted in TONNES per day (int64), matching §33's 'all freight accounted in tonnes/day end-to-end'. A freight commodity whose 'unit' is 'kWh' or 'L' (power, fuel) is tracked for chain completeness and priced via its mapped engine.market commodity, but is EXCLUDED from the tonnes-conservation identity (AC-10) — that identity covers only unit=='tonne' commodities.",
    "marketMappingConvention": "Every freight commodity carries a 'market' field naming one of the nine engine.market CommodityType keys (data/market.json) it is priced and availability-bounded through (AC-8), and a 'unitsPerTonne' field: the number of market units in one freight tonne (1000 for kg-priced food/consumer goods, 1 for tonne-priced construction materials). Export/import value = tonnes * unitsPerTonne * market.Price(market). MarketAPI exposes no separate non-waste export price (data/market.json prices importable commodities once), so the static market price is the value basis for BOTH directions pending M2 pricing (ASM, see doc.go).",
    "balanceNote": "All port/customs/storage/chain figures are COARSE PLACEHOLDERS (unpinned balance data pending M2 tuning, per the acceptance doc's Escalations) chosen only to exercise the model. The modal caps (road 25t, rail 1000t, sea 3-40kt) are the spec-stated magnitudes §33/§8 names; everything else is directional.",
    "storageClassConvention": "Four storage-site types (§33): quayside stacks (general), silos (grain), tank farm (fuel), cold store (fresh/fish). A freight commodity's 'storageClass' must match the site's 'commodityClass'; routing a commodity to a mismatched site is rejected (AC-6)."
  },
  "port": {
    "berths": 2,
    "craneRateTonnesPerHour": 60,
    "operatingHoursPerDay": 16,
    "customsCapacityTonnesPerDay": 1500,
    "comment": "Port physical throughput = berths * craneRateTonnesPerHour * operatingHoursPerDay (§33, AC-2). Customs throughput is a SEPARATE capacity figure (§33/§28, AC-3); the two saturate independently."
  },
